                    <h4 class="mb-3">Overview</h4>
                    <p>
                        This interface allows you to create entries for <strong>CONSIGNEE</strong>, 
                        <strong>PACKAGE</strong>, and <strong>COURIER</strong> sync types.
                    </p>
                    <p>
    <strong>CONSIGNEE</strong> pulls data from your system into the warehouse. Required fields are:
    <code>first_name</code>, <code>last_name</code>, and <code>mailbox</code>. 
    <br>
    The following fields are optional: <code>branch</code> and <code>email</code>.
</p>
<p>An array of objects is required.Active false will result in deletion</p>
<p>
The API-KEY/KEY you provide is sent with each request in the header as 'API-KEY',please use the form at the bottom of this page to enter,select KEY and then create courier sync
</p>
<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px;">
    <h2>API Key Authentication & Webhook Setup</h2>

    <p>
        The API key you provide is included with every request in the
        <strong>HTTP header</strong> as a <strong>Bearer token</strong>.
        This key is used to securely identify and authorize your system when it
        communicates with the API.
    </p>

    <h3>How it works</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>You issue an <strong>API key(not the api key for endpoints,webhooks use the api key you provide)</strong>.</li>
        <li>Each request to the API must include this key in the request header.</li>
        <li>The server verifies the key and processes the request.</li>
        <li>Each uuid is deterministic from a hash.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Header Format</h3>
    <pre style="background:#f4f4f4; padding:12px; border-radius:6px;">
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY
    </pre>

    <h3>Example using cURL</h3>
    <pre style="background:#f4f4f4; padding:12px; border-radius:6px;">
curl -X POST https://api.example.com/courier/sync \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer 1234567890abcdef" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"sample":"data"}'
    </pre>

    <h3>Creating a Webhook (Sync Setup)</h3>
    <p>
        To receive automatic updates from the system, you must create a
        <strong>sync</strong> (webhook) for the data type you want.
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li>Use the form at the bottom of this page.</li>
        <li>Enter your <strong>API key</strong>.</li>
        <li>Select <strong>KEY</strong> as the sync type.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Create Sync</strong>.</li>
     </ol>
<p>
        
    </p>
You must select **Package** for the package webhook and create the sync. Do the same for **Collection**, **Consignee**, and any other required sync types.


    <p>
        Once created, the system will automatically send updates for the selected
        sync type (e.g., packages) to your configured endpoint using your API key.
    </p>
</div>

